/* ============================================================
   SPECIES — which fish are in which water, for the species filter.
   Generated from ~/.cache/flyfish-osm/species/ (build.py, then apply.py):
   edit the pipeline and re-run it, never this file.

   A species is listed for a water only when a fisheries agency or the
   park says so for that water (WGFD's Fishing Guide, IDFG's Fishing
   Planner, the Iowa DNR's stream and lake pages, Yellowstone's 2026
   regulations), or when the water's own regulation entry has a rule
   about that species. Never from region, never from memory.

     SPECIES_LIST   the picker's species, in order: {key, label, short, group}
     SPECIES_SRC    srcKey -> {name, url, date, page?, checked?, regs?}.
                    page: the agency page's own title (one source per page
                    for the per-water pages). date: when the source was
                    last updated, or with checked, the day it was read.
                    regs: the species is named in the water's own
                    regulations, which ranks below agency data and is used
                    only where no agency source gives that species.
     SPECIES_SCOPE  what has been built so far: states, regions and the
                    PARK_INFO rows of the lakes covered. A water inside it
                    with no entry has been looked for and has no data yet.
     SPECIES        river id, or "lake:" + lake id (the Field Book's
                    keys) -> [[species, srcKey, how, note], ...]; how is
                    "wild", "stocked" or null (not stated), note is the
                    source's own words (a subspecies, a survey year).
   ============================================================ */
